 "title": "13 of 41 backdoors no monitor caught look suspicious to Opus",
 "section": "appendix",
 "order": 121,
 "caption": "The ten highest-scored backdoors among the 41 that no monitor caught. Bars are Opus 5.5 at xhigh effort. Each row label is the problem id and, in brackets, what Sonnet and Haiku gave the same backdoor. Those two never go above 4 on any of them.",
 "notes": [
  "Opus scores the other 31 missed backdoors at 27 or below, median 2, so this is a tail rather than a general advantage.",
  "Opus never saw honest code here, so a high score is not a catch. Without its own honest distribution there is no cutoff to compare these against.",
  "P12 carries this finding in the report as a share of the whole set. This figure is the per-backdoor detail behind it, kept in the appendix.",
  "Ported from scripts/analysis_opus_hard51.py, which drew this as opus-hard51-fig2-missed.png."
